{"id":"20260828T234650.056000152Z-122e8105","time":"2026-08-28T23:46:50.056000152Z","session_id":"session-20260828T234642.377555027Z","task_id":"task-1787960802377933262","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  The Level-1 routine classifier reads coverage for the whole planned region; make it read the per-file fact the authority router already records, so a plan holding a file the graph never examined is never classified routine.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended with an externally supplied plan; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] classifyRoutine reads scoped.Coverage.Proven(), a region-level verdict, at routine.go condition 3. (internal/workflow/routine.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] routingRecord holds Policy, Scoped, Claims and Planned, and no per-file coverage fact. (internal/workflow/engine.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Action.Unexamined is established per file at routing and is available where setRouting is called. (internal/workflow/engine.go) — source: repository\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: architectural-authority-granted\n"}
{"id":"20260828T234650.056183769Z-ed7f21bd","time":"2026-08-28T23:46:50.056183769Z","session_id":"session-20260828T234642.377555027Z","task_id":"task-1787960802377933262","source":"system","kind":"plan.proposed","summary":"Supplied plan (not architect-produced; sha256 3cc668d80a8b603ca81828aecb4697d71472b7c16898332bd1af741bd17349f0)\nThe Level-1 routine classifier reads coverage for the whole planned region; make it read the per-file fact the authority router already records, so a plan holding a file the graph never examined is never classified routine.\n\nPlan:\n  1. Add the unexamined planned files to routingRecord and record them in setRouting from the action that was routed.\n  2. Add one blocking condition to classifyRoutine: any planned file the graph never examined blocks, naming the file; a record with none behaves as today.\n  3. In ClassifyCounterfactual, where no routing record exists, record the new condition as assumed, as conditions 8 and 9 are.\n  4. Add a regression test in internal/workflow/routine_test.go: a region-proven scoped preflight with one unexamined planned file is not routine, and the same preflight with none unexamined classifies as before.\n  5. Run gofmt -l cmd internal, go vet ./..., and go test ./... .","payload":{"decision":"proceed","summary":"The Level-1 routine classifier reads coverage for the whole planned region; make it read the per-file fact the authority router already records, so a plan holding a file the graph never examined is never classified routine.","steps":["Add the unexamined planned files to routingRecord and record them in setRouting from the action that was routed.","Add one blocking condition to classifyRoutine: any planned file the graph never examined blocks, naming the file; a record with none behaves as today.","In ClassifyCounterfactual, where no routing record exists, record the new condition as assumed, as conditions 8 and 9 are.","Add a regression test in internal/workflow/routine_test.go: a region-proven scoped preflight with one unexamined planned file is not routine, and the same preflight with none unexamined classifies as before.","Run gofmt -l cmd internal, go vet ./..., and go test ./... ."],"consequences":"A plan carrying a file the graph never examined can no longer be classified routine on its neighbour's anchors; plans with every file examined classify exactly as before. No routing, authority or admission behaviour changes.","files":["internal/workflow/engine.go","internal/workflow/routine.go","internal/workflow/routine_scan.go","internal/workflow/routine_test.go"],"mode":"modify","plan":"routingRecord (internal/workflow/engine.go) carries only the region-level scoped preflight; classifyRoutine (internal/workflow/routine.go) reads scoped.Coverage.Proven() for the region, which is proven the moment one planned file carries anchors. Carry the router's per-file fact -- the unexamined architectural files established at routing -- on routingRecord, set it where setRouting records the routing evidence, and make classifyRoutine block when any planned file is unexamined, naming the file. ClassifyCounterfactual (internal/workflow/routine_scan.go) has no routing record, so it records the condition as assumed rather than tested, like conditions 8 and 9. Add the regression test beside the existing routine tests. No change in any other behaviour.","claims":[{"statement":"classifyRoutine reads scoped.Coverage.Proven(), a region-level verdict, at routine.go condition 3.","about":"internal/workflow/routine.go","source":"repository"},{"statement":"routingRecord holds Policy, Scoped, Claims and Planned, and no per-file coverage fact.","about":"internal/workflow/engine.go","source":"repository"},{"statement":"Action.Unexamined is established per file at routing and is available where setRouting is called.","about":"internal/workflow/engine.go","source":"repository"}],"plan_source":"supplied","plan_digest":"3cc668d80a8b603ca81828aecb4697d71472b7c16898332bd1af741bd17349f0"}}
