{"id":"20260828T234831.645595013Z-1a1b5139","time":"2026-08-28T23:48:31.645595013Z","session_id":"session-20260828T234642.377555027Z","task_id":"task-1787960802377933262","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeW3JRTt6s8yatpySoTEw\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Done. Committed as `00ffbfd` on the candidate branch.\\n\\n**What changed**\\n1. `internal/workflow/engine.go` — `routingRecord` gains `Unexamined []string`; `setRouting` now takes the routed `Action` and records `action.unexaminedArchitecturalFiles()`. All three call sites pass the action (the `escalate` branch previously discarded it with `_`; it now captures it).\\n2. `internal/workflow/routine.go` — `classifyRoutine` takes `unexamined []string` and adds condition **3b** right after the region-coverage check: any unexamined planned file blocks with `the plan names a file the graph never examined: \u003cfiles\u003e`; none → held as `every planned file was examined by the graph`. The dark run passes `record.Unexamined`. `generalise()` groups the new reason.\\n3. `internal/workflow/routine_scan.go` — `ClassifyCounterfactual` passes `nil` and always records `3b: … (no routing record carries the per-file fact)` as assumed, beside 8 and 9.\\n4. `internal/workflow/routine_test.go` — `TestAPlanHoldingAnUnexaminedFileIsNeverRoutine`: a region-proven preflight (anchors=3, files=2, indexed=1, sufficient) with one unexamined planned file blocks and names the file; the same preflight with none unexamined is routine. The all-conditions count test moves from 9 to 10; other call sites (incl. two live tests, `adversarial_test.go`) pass `nil`/`Action{}`.\\n\\n**Verification**: `gofmt -l cmd internal` clean; `go vet ./...` clean; `go test ./...` passes everywhere except `internal/publish` `TestCommitAndPushReachARealRemote`, which fails only because this worker session's push guard refuses pushes — environmental, not caused by this change.\\n\\n**Judgement calls worth the architect's eye**: the new condition is numbered 3b (not 10) so conditions 4–9 keep their names in docs and the assumed-list; and `ClassifyCounterfactual` now *always* carries one assumed entry, so `Counterfactual.Trustworthy()` is never true on the scan path — which is honest (no per-file fact exists there) but changes the trust tally's meaning. Nothing outside the plan was touched.\\n\\nAWG: briefing(internal/workflow/routine.go, engine.go, routine_scan.go) | invariants: relax interruptions never evidence; per-file fact engine-owned, never read off the region answer | uncertainty: Trustworthy() now always false on the counterfactual scan path\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":56,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":657,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":57969,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":657},\"output_tokens\":5,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"a5f35a98-b0e9-43d8-bb7b-a2be56f633c9\",\"uuid\":\"a8729632-0a5e-4c09-8697-8e61581864a2\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-28T23:48:31.629Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CeW3JNvat16SrszBdpWVF\"}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
